From 10f0078e5b847f25452b0646215e4635c913d4ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Paunovic <royalnet026@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 16:09:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: extend 420 pixel-phase lock wait in DCE
 formatter reset

On an RK3588 (arm64) host driving a Polaris card over PCIe Gen3 x4,
the FMT_420_PIXEL_PHASE_LOCKED poll routinely exceeds its 100us budget
when the DIG resync FIFO is reprogrammed for YCbCr 4:2:0 output
(4K60 HDR over HDMI 2.0). The timeout leaves the FIFO unaligned,
shifting pixel phase and producing a green-tinted image; during early
boot modesets the same failure can wedge the whole display init.

Extend the wait to a 100ms worst-case budget. REG_WAIT returns as soon
as the phase locks, so the common (fast-lock) case is unaffected.

Observed and diagnosed on Orange Pi 5 Plus + XFX RX 580 8GB eGPU:
every HDR toggle logged exactly one
'REG_WAIT timeout 10us * 10 tries - program_formatter_reset_dig_resync_fifo'
and DisplayPort HDR output (which bypasses this path) shows correct
colors on the same setup.

Signed-off-by: Igor Paunovic <royalnet026@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dce/dce_opp.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dce/dce_opp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dce/dce_opp.c
index f342da5a5..0b424a4cc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dce/dce_opp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/dce/dce_opp.c
@@ -642,8 +642,12 @@ static void program_formatter_reset_dig_resync_fifo(struct output_pixel_processo
 	REG_UPDATE(FMT_CONTROL,
 			FMT_420_PIXEL_PHASE_LOCKED_CLEAR, 1);
 
-	/* poll until FMT_420_PIXEL_PHASE_LOCKED become 1*/
-	REG_WAIT(FMT_CONTROL, FMT_420_PIXEL_PHASE_LOCKED, 1, 10, 10);
+	/* poll until FMT_420_PIXEL_PHASE_LOCKED become 1
+	 * RK3588 eGPU: the 420 pixel-phase takes longer to lock than the
+	 * stock 100us budget; a short timeout leaves the FIFO unaligned and
+	 * produces a green-tinted image on YCbCr 4:2:0 output (e.g. 4K60 HDR
+	 * over HDMI 2.0). Give it real headroom - it returns early on lock. */
+	REG_WAIT(FMT_CONTROL, FMT_420_PIXEL_PHASE_LOCKED, 1, 50, 2000);
 
 }
 
